    "id":  15692,
    "title":  "Band-9 Samples: How often do you make telephone calls? [Why/Why not?]",
    "slug":  "cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9",
    "link":  "https://engnovate.com/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9/",
    "date":  "2023-08-21T23:13:57",
    "content":  "\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eThis post contains ideas and band-9 sample answers (audio included) for the\u0026nbsp;\u003cem\u003eCambridge IELTS 9 Academic Speaking Part 1 Question 1 Test 3\u003c/em\u003e\u0026nbsp;question:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003e“How often do you make telephone calls? [Why/Why not?]”\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 1: Regularly\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-1.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-1.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI frequently use the phone for work-related reasons, at least three or five times a day. In my occupation, it\u0026#8217;s crucial to maintain clear lines of communication with my colleagues, so I regularly make and receive calls, even if it\u0026#8217;s just for a brief check-in.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 2: Regularly\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-2.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-2.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI make phone calls quite a lot, mainly because my family lives in a different city. I find that talking to them over the phone helps bridge the physical distance, and it\u0026#8217;s a nice way to keep up with their lives.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 3: Regularly\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-3.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-3.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI dial numbers quite regularly, primarily to keep in touch with my friends. We are all quite busy, so grabbing a coffee or meeting up isn\u0026#8217;t always feasible. A quick phone call helps us stay connected and catch up on each other\u0026#8217;s lives.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 4: Moderately\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-4.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-4.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI usually reach out to people via the phone on a balanced basis, not too frequently, nor too rarely. My career in consulting demands a fair amount of telephone conversations, but I tend to reserve my calls for those matters that require a more in-depth discussion or a personal touch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 5: Moderately\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-5.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-5.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI make phone calls moderately. As an entrepreneur, I have to juggle a lot of balls. While telephone calls are essential for business, I prefer to keep them to a minimum to avoid disruptions in my workflow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 6: Moderately\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-6.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-6.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI ring up people moderately because I believe in meaningful conversations rather than frequent ones. I prefer to engage in dialogues that add value and are not just a routine or a way to pass the time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 7: Rarely\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-7.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-7.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI seldom make telephone calls since I\u0026#8217;m a big fan of face-to-face communication. There\u0026#8217;s something about seeing the other person\u0026#8217;s facial expressions and body language that just makes the conversation more meaningful and authentic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 8: Rarely\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-8.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-8.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI don\u0026#8217;t usually make many phone calls due to my hectic professional life. My job consumes a large portion of my day, and I barely have time for leisurely chats. I mostly resort to quick texts or emails for necessary communication.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 9: Rarely\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-9.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-9.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eI rarely make phone calls because I tend to lean more toward digital communication platforms like email or social media. They provide a more convenient and quicker way to exchange information, especially when dealing with multiple tasks at the same time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"\u003eSample 10: It Depends\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-female-voice-10.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eFemale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"wp-block-audio\"\u003e\u003caudio controls src=\"https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/cambridge-ielts-9-academic-speaking-part-1-question-1-test-3-samples-band-9-male-voice-10.mp3\"\u003e\u003c/audio\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"\u003eMale\u003c/figcaption\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"\u003eFor me, the frequency of making phone calls is seasonal. During festive times or holidays, I tend to make a lot of calls to connect with family and friends. But outside of these periods, I\u0026#8217;m not really one to often engage in telephone conversations.\u003c/p\u003e\n",
    "excerpt":  "\u003cp\u003eThis post contains ideas and band-9 sample answers (audio included) for the\u0026nbsp;Cambridge IELTS 9 Academic Speaking Part 1 Question 1 Test 3\u0026nbsp;question: “How often do you make telephone calls? [Why/Why not?]” Sample 1: Regularly I frequently use the phone for work-related reasons, at least three or five times a day. In my occupation, it\u0026#8217;s crucial [\u0026hellip;]\u003c/p\u003e\n"
}
